What is taken from franc-min 6.2.0:
  - The set of supported languages (the keys of data.js and expressions.js)
    and their ISO 639-3 codes. English names follow the ISO 639-3
    reference names listed in the franc-min readme, without the
    parenthesised qualifiers.
  - The Unicode ranges of each script in script_ranges.mbt, decoded from
    the regular expressions in franc-min 6.2.0 expressions.js
    (https://unpkg.com/franc-min@6.2.0/expressions.js): surrogate pairs
    were combined into code points and adjacent ranges merged, without
    adding or removing any code point. The script order used to break
    ties is the key order of that file.

Universal Declaration of Human Rights
  franc builds its trigram profiles from translations of the Universal
  Declaration of Human Rights collected by the UDHR in Unicode project
  (https://unicode.org/udhr/). Any trigram data in this repository is
  derived from franc-min 6.2.0 and therefore from that corpus.
